68 #edb/ref 17592186406783 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406787 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182007" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406787 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406787 #edb/ref 1071 "Complete the following reasoning about the set $S=(7,\\infty ):$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406787 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f612405e-da38-57fe-9f2c-b87a69f932d8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406787 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if \n\n- ${x}_{min}\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nIn our case, the value $7$ is not the minimum of the set $S$ because $7\\notin S.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406775 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406777 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182027" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A=(-2,1)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7921076-6399-562d-b241-b9adcf057407" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406788 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that $-2\\notin A$ and $1\\notin A.$ So, we have the following:\n\n- $min(A)=min(-2,1),$ which $\\text{does not exist}$\n\n- $max(A)=max(-2,1),$ which $\\text{does not exist}$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406780 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406781 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181993" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $C={1,\\,-8,\\,7,\\,2}?$\n\n$min(C)=$\n\n$-8$\n\n$\\,max(C)=$\n\n$7$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f87da9b9-2a22-52c7-9a6b-99820a90343e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406789 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(C) & =min{1,\\,-8,\\,7,\\,2}=-8 \\\\ max(C) & =max{1,\\,-8,\\,7,\\,2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
